Package: tretlager
Version: @VERSION@
Architecture: all
Section: games
Priority: optional
Maintainer: Christoph Langner <mail@christoph-langner.de>
Installed-Size: @SIZE@
Depends: python3 (>= 3.12), python3-bleak, python3-dbus-fast, python3-secretstorage,
 python3-pyside6.qtcore, python3-pyside6.qtdbus, python3-pyside6.qtgui, python3-pyside6.qtqml, python3-pyside6.qtquick,
 python3-pyside6.qtquickcontrols2, qml6-module-org-kde-kirigami, qml6-module-org-kde-kirigamiaddons-formcard,
 qml6-module-org-kde-kirigamiaddons-components, qml6-module-qtquick-layouts,
 python3-pyside6.qtwebenginequick, qml6-module-qtwebengine,
 qml6-module-qtquick-controls, qml6-module-qtquick-effects, qml6-module-qtquick-dialogs,
 qml6-module-qtquick-window, qml6-module-qtcore, qml6-module-org-kde-desktop, breeze-icon-theme, breeze,
 avahi-daemon, bluez, pkexec, gpg, osslsigncode, cabextract, systemd
Recommends: plasma-integration
Description: Set up Zwift on Linux, launch it and connect your sensors
 Tretlager sets up the official Windows client of Zwift under Wine (WineHQ),
 verifies the installer's signature, picks the graphics path (NVIDIA via PRIME
 offload) and launches Zwift with one click.
 .
 The sensor bridge connects smart trainers and heart rate straps via BlueZ and
 offers them to Zwift as Wahoo Direct Connect devices, without Zwift Companion.
 .
 Zwift does not officially support Linux. The optional sign-in via the browser
 violates the Zwift terms of service and is at your own risk.
